  "q": "[image not available offline] Examine the figure above of the pulmonary and systemic circulations. Describe the structural and functional differences between the two circulations. THREE obvious misconceptions are present in these answers. Find them and give the correct answers to rectify the misconceptions. ANSWER WITH MISCONCEPTIONS The pulmonary system connects and delivers oxygenated blood to the lungs and returns deoxygenated blood to the heart. The systemic circuit delivers oxygenated blood to the body for the purpose of cellular activity and drains deoxygenated blood from the lungs and from the rest of the body . The lung tissue gets oxygen from the pulmonary system.",
